# Root build context for the trainer image (docker-compose `trainer` service
# builds from here so it can copy BOTH friendy_chachkalica/ and chachak/ in a
# repo-root layout — chachak imports friendy_chachkalica as a package). Keep the
# context lean: the Django app tree, data, venvs, and git history are irrelevant
# to the trainer image and huge.
chachkalica/
.git/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/data/
**/runs/
*.pt
.env

# Same reasoning for buildnode/Dockerfile, which shares this context. It needs
# chachak/, onnx_infer/, trt_infer/, part of friendy_chachkalica/, buildnode/ and
# models/people/detector*.onnx — and nothing else. These are large and are only
# ever used through a bind mount at runtime (person_model_test holds the person
# checkpoint that make_person_graphs.py reads), never COPYed into an image.
person_model_test/
dist/
logs/

# inferlica/ is NOT excluded, despite the note above: the trainer image now COPYs it
# (the bundle benchmark runs from it — see friendy_chachkalica/Dockerfile). It is a few
# hundred KB of Python with __pycache__ already excluded, so the cost to the buildnode
# image, which shares this context and does not copy it, is only the context transfer.
